[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: scribe move renames on disk outside Graph, pending and save

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SCRIBE-MOVE-BYPASSES-THE-MODEL
TITLE: scribe move renames on disk outside Graph, pending and save
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
`scribe move` renames the file on disk directly and then verifies, bypassing
Graph, pending() and save() entirely (sdoc_cli.py:461-478). A handler anchored
on the save path -- which is where every other write goes -- never sees a move,
and the library form has no move at all. Measured 2026-08-28 while inventorying
scribe's phases for the hook layer.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Dry-run delivery record retained when its completed WORK row was retired on
2026-09-10. A move preserves source bytes and previews only its rename. Both
the real and dry-run paths touch, render, and reparse the source before rename,
so both refuse a document that does not round-trip. Graph.touch_document is
the public mutation seam used for that validation.
<<<
